<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Glaxo Wellcome lowered.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Glaxo Wellcome lowered.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- Gruntal said analysts David Saks and Adam Greene cut Glaxo Wellcome Plc to an outperform long-term rating from outperform.  </p>
<p>-- said cut was based on reduced EPS estimates, stock valuation and uncertainty over generic competition.</p>
<p>-- cut 1997 earnings estimate to $1.85 a share from $2.00.</p>
<p>-- cut 1998 estimate to $1.95 a share from $2.30.</p>
<p>-- company earned $1.77 a share in 1996.</p>
<p>-- set two-year target price of $45.</p>
<p>-- stock traded down 5/8 to 36-1/4 in morning trade.</p>
</text>
